00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.510 align:start position:0%
the european union's general affairs  council has kicked off serbia's eu  membership talks with the first official  round of negotiations to start next  month  they adopted negotiation framework for  serbia that means we started de facto  negotiations  and we are looking forward to the first  intergovernmental conference which will  take place in january  like all candidates for membership  serbia will have to meet eu standards in  35 policy areas or chapters the process  can take several years  in a broader look at eu enlargement the  ministers also said that granting  albania's request for candidate status  was just a question of time and that  this could happen in june  the former yugoslav republic of  macedonia's hopes of beginning accession  talks will be considered again next year  the ministers also debated a review of  the european external action service  they gave their full support to  recommendations that could be  implemented in the short term like  boosting cooperation between eu  delegations and those of the member  states and acknowledge the need to  improve the effectiveness of common  security and defence policy missions  the ministers also had a working lunch  with president herman van rompuy to  discuss preparations for this week's  european council in brussels eu leaders  are set to discuss defence policy and  europe's defence industry economic  policy the fate of would-be immigrants  in the mediterranean as well as  relations with ukraine and the central  african republic
 

